/*
 * The text the widget gallery and the widget cards show, for one locale.
 *
 * Generated from app/lib/l10n/app_eo.arb, the one catalogue both platforms
 * read: the widget names and `habit_not_found` are the same strings
 * android/app/src/main/res/values-<locale>/strings.xml mirrors for the
 * Android widgets (audit.android-widget-chrome-text-is-hard#1). A widget
 * extension cannot read the ARB files — it runs outside the Flutter engine, in the
 * widget gallery's process, often before the app has ever launched — so the
 * translations travel as a compiled `.strings` table instead.
 *
 * Every key appears in every table. A key missing from a localized table is
 * not resolved against English: iOS hands the key itself back, and the user
 * reads "widget_name_checkmark" on their home screen.
 */

